// The tower's living core. Pre-placed, unique, and cannot be removed.
// From M2 its destruction ends the run.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
RoomDef(
    id: "room.heartseed",
    name: "Heartseed",
    short: "❤",
    category: Heart,
    // Three slots. It is the tower's reason for walking and the
    // thing everything else is arranged around, so it should take up
    // the room a hearth takes up.
    width: 3,
    unique: true,
    // **Two shelves, because a seed carries its own stores.**
    //
    // M6 cut the opening tower to a bed and two floors (`SYSTEMS.md`
    // §6.11), and `starting_stock` has to live somewhere: a build cost
    // is paid off a shelf, so a tower with no shelves cannot build the
    // first thing it is asked to build. A pre-placed storeroom would
    // have done it, and would also have eaten the only three
    // contiguous slots on the ground floor — which is where a salvage
    // rig goes, and a rig is three wide and reaches the ground.
    //
    // **Three, and the number is the opening ladder's arithmetic.** A
    // shelf takes whichever item lands on it first and holds only that
    // kind, and by the time a storeroom is affordable the tower has
    // made exactly three materials: the poles it set out with, the
    // bamboo the cutter arm strips, and the resin feedstock the farm grows.
    // Two shelves deadlocked on that — measured on the golden
    // recorder, 20 bamboo and 3 resin feedstock holding both shelves while the
    // mill's poles had nowhere to land and the storeroom that would
    // have fixed it cost three of them.
    //
    // Three rather than four, and 60 against a storeroom's 80: enough
    // that the opening cannot jam itself, nowhere near enough to save
    // with. The storeroom is still the room you build when you want to
    // keep things, which is what makes shelf space a decision.
    storage: StorageDef(
        shelves: 3,
        per_shelf: 20,
    ),
)
